      "message": "Whenever I\u0027m touching code in tools/idea, I generally leave the code I removed (or changed) there in place and just comment it out instead, with a specific comment explaining why we\u0027ve made a deliberate change in Android Studio. That makes future merges easier (and you can generally grep the codebase looking for Android Studio specific tweaks). Take a look at groovy/src/META-INF/plugin.xml for example.\n\n(This is different from when we\u0027re making a change that we expect JetBrains to want for IntelliJ as well; in that case, just send them a patch instead -- I\u0027m talking about the case where we\u0027re changing the way the base IDE works for some specific version).",
